SUMMARY:Columbia Slough Watershed Council Free Community Events (Slough Sci
 ence & Bird Walks): Bird Walk at Smith and Bybee Wetlands
DESCRIPTION:Category: Parks & Nature\nCost: FREE\nInfo: Guided morning bird
  walk with Ryan Gilpin along a gentle paved trail to a wheelchair-accessib
 le viewing platform. Extra binoculars\, snacks\, and drinks provided. No d
 ogs.\nAddress: 7040 NE 47th Ave\, Portland\, OR 97218\nPhone: 503-281-1132
 \nWebsite: https://www.columbiaslough.org/events\nDetails: Free environmen
 tal education\, bird walks\, and watershed tours in North and Northeast Po
 rtland and Gresham through Q1 2027.
LOCATION:Smith and Bybee Wetlands Natural Area (meet at the boat launch pas
 t main parking lot)\, 5300 N Marine Dr\, Portland\, OR 97203
URL:https://www.columbiaslough.org/events
CATEGORIES:Parks & Nature
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
